WEBVTT

01:30.980 --> 01:35.990
<b>Episode 4</b>

01:30.980 --> 01:35.990
<b>When Monsters Attack,
Unpreparedness Is the Greatest Enemy</b>

01:42.770 --> 01:44.550
<i>What is magic?</i>

01:44.550 --> 01:47.830
<i>Magic is the most advanced art in this world.</i>

01:48.460 --> 01:53.160
<i>Nations compete to determine 
who best utilizes its power.</i>

01:56.850 --> 02:01.510
And magic stones, like this one, 
are the core of every magic tool.

02:02.230 --> 02:06.130
This magic wand is made 
with a magic stone, as well.

02:07.000 --> 02:12.020
It was magic stones that led 
to the invention of magic tools.

02:12.470 --> 02:14.540
Magic users can bring about 
all sorts of phenomena

02:14.540 --> 02:17.030
depending on the strength of their magic.

02:17.750 --> 02:20.010
The greater and purer one's magic is,

02:20.010 --> 02:22.860
the greater the phenomena 
they are capable of.

02:24.410 --> 02:28.910
The mining and distribution of magic stones 
is nationally regulated.

02:28.910 --> 02:31.870
In this nation, they are managed 
by the Aurousseau Company

02:31.870 --> 02:34.610
with the permission of the royal family.

02:34.610 --> 02:37.500
That's my Lene's household.

02:38.170 --> 02:43.800
Now, for today's lesson, 
you'll fire some actual magic shots.

02:43.800 --> 02:47.680
You can imagine that the targets are monsters.

02:55.330 --> 02:59.400
<i>Monsters first appeared along with 
the discovery of magic stones.</i>

02:59.980 --> 03:02.960
<i>They are animals that have taken 
magic stones into their bodies,</i>

03:02.960 --> 03:06.100
<i>drastically changing their 
shapes and appearances.</i>

03:06.100 --> 03:09.160
<i>A monster's weakness is the magic 
stone that serves as its core.</i>

03:10.270 --> 03:11.420
<i>Right, then.</i>

03:18.300 --> 03:21.970
Rae, you've been in your 
own world this whole time.

03:21.970 --> 03:23.290
Are you all right?

03:23.820 --> 03:26.130
Oh, sorry. I zoned out.

03:26.130 --> 03:27.800
I swear...

03:27.800 --> 03:32.610
You may be a dual caster, 
but you can't neglect daily practice.

03:32.610 --> 03:33.690
Yeah, you're right.

03:34.600 --> 03:38.430
Let's see... Magic shot, magic shot...

03:38.430 --> 03:39.290
There.

03:50.710 --> 03:52.100
Wow...

03:52.100 --> 03:54.640
That's what someone with 
two attributes is capable of?

03:54.640 --> 03:57.480
<i>Shoot! I misjudged the strength I needed!</i>

03:57.480 --> 03:59.550
<i>This is another case of...</i>

03:59.550 --> 04:02.420
<i>I just blew it again, didn't I?!</i>

04:10.580 --> 04:12.580
Don't get too full of yourself!

04:12.580 --> 04:16.060
It doesn't take a dual caster 
to pull that off!

04:16.060 --> 04:17.800
Miss Claire...

04:17.800 --> 04:20.070
Oh, dear. You're so upset, you're crying?

04:20.070 --> 04:22.300
You're so awesome! Please marry me!

04:22.300 --> 04:24.000
How did that lead to this?!

04:24.000 --> 04:26.070
Come, now. Don't lose focus.

04:26.800 --> 04:28.270
Mr. Torrid...

04:28.270 --> 04:32.340
Magic is a dangerous art if used incorrectly.

04:32.340 --> 04:34.550
You must be very careful and very serious.

04:34.550 --> 04:35.330
Sorry.

04:35.330 --> 04:36.790
I apologize, sir.

04:38.690 --> 04:39.840
What?

04:39.840 --> 04:46.130
You're really able to show true respect 
to someone better than you, huh?

04:46.130 --> 04:48.070
I love that about you, too.

04:48.070 --> 04:49.600
Of course I can.

04:50.030 --> 04:51.680
Mr. Torrid was one of the pioneers

04:51.680 --> 04:54.600
who established the foundations 
of magic in this kingdom.

04:54.890 --> 05:04.110
<b>m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100</b>

04:54.890 --> 05:04.110
<b>Torrid Magic</b>

04:55.100 --> 04:57.180
Though his aptitude is only intermediate,

04:57.180 --> 05:00.300
he commands the attributes 
of fire, earth, and water,

05:00.300 --> 05:03.320
making him the kingdom's 
one and only tri-caster!

05:04.110 --> 05:07.670
Even a commoner like you must know that!

05:07.670 --> 05:09.910
Of course I'm aware of that.

05:09.910 --> 05:12.600
This kingdom lagged 
behind the others in magic,

05:12.600 --> 05:14.750
and then he appeared, like a comet!

05:14.750 --> 05:17.000
He is truly the father of magic!

05:17.620 --> 05:19.510
Y-Yes, I get it!

05:19.510 --> 05:21.990
Stop doing that weird pose!

05:22.570 --> 05:23.630
<i>I don't know them.</i>

05:34.620 --> 05:38.900
Next, I will explain the magical attributes.

05:38.900 --> 05:43.400
<b>Water</b>

05:38.900 --> 05:43.400
<b>Wind</b>

05:38.900 --> 05:43.400
<b>Fire</b>

05:38.900 --> 05:43.400
<b>Earth</b>

05:39.370 --> 05:43.400
<i>There are four attributes, 
each with its own affinities.</i>

05:43.990 --> 05:46.030
<i>Earth is strong against wind,</i>

05:46.430 --> 05:48.530
<i>wind is strong against water,</i>

05:48.530 --> 05:50.780
<i>fire is strong against earth,</i>

05:50.780 --> 05:53.040
<i>and water is strong against fire.</i>

05:53.550 --> 05:58.040
<i>Of course, that's not strictly absolute. 
There are exceptions.</i>

05:58.040 --> 06:02.470
There are other ways in which the attributes 
can be broadly categorized, as well.

06:02.470 --> 06:03.960
For example...

06:05.480 --> 06:07.590
Earth magic can defend.

06:09.050 --> 06:11.310
You can create a wall of earth, like this.

06:11.310 --> 06:16.100
Advanced users can even 
build entire castle walls.

06:16.100 --> 06:18.270
Fire magic can attack.

06:19.760 --> 06:22.190
Water magic can heal.

06:22.740 --> 06:25.940
It can be used to treat 
injuries and illnesses.

06:26.450 --> 06:29.970
The dead, however, 
cannot be brought back to life.

06:31.450 --> 06:37.580
And wind magic, which I can't use, 
primarily fills supportive roles.

06:38.390 --> 06:41.940
<i>Combining an attribute with fire 
increases its attack power,</i>

06:45.020 --> 06:48.760
<i>while combining one with water 
increases its healing capabilities.</i>

06:51.640 --> 06:53.210
<i>That about covers it.</i>

06:53.990 --> 06:56.260
Now, let's put this into actual practice.

06:56.260 --> 06:59.780
I will advise those of you with 
the wind attribute individually,

06:59.780 --> 07:01.900
so please come to me.

07:12.780 --> 07:16.210
An earth wall... Kinda like this?

07:32.140 --> 07:34.850
Still such good buddies, aren't you?

07:35.240 --> 07:37.700
Prince Rod! Prince Yu!

07:38.100 --> 07:39.930
You are gravely mistaken!

07:39.930 --> 07:43.340
I have not befriended this 
person in the slightest!

07:43.340 --> 07:44.730
You heard her, Rae.

07:45.040 --> 07:46.940
That's why I love Miss Claire!

07:46.940 --> 07:48.480
You shut up!

07:49.830 --> 07:50.990
Anyway...

07:51.410 --> 07:53.220
Where is Prince Thane?

07:53.220 --> 07:56.130
Oh, he's with Mr. Torrid.

08:01.400 --> 08:04.760
You really blasted that target. Nice going.

08:05.430 --> 08:08.740
We're not that great at magic ourselves,

08:08.740 --> 08:10.490
so we kinda envy you.

08:10.490 --> 08:11.260
Huh.

08:11.260 --> 08:14.920
Does it not make you happy to 
be praised by Their Highnesses?

08:14.920 --> 08:16.640
Actually...

08:16.640 --> 08:20.060
Being complimented by you 
would make me far happier!

08:21.140 --> 08:23.540
That is <i>never</i> going to happen!

08:23.540 --> 08:25.640
You two really are good buddies.

08:25.640 --> 08:30.280
By the way, are you two gonna take 
the Academy Knights exam next week?

08:30.280 --> 08:31.250
Huh?

08:31.250 --> 08:35.640
Brother, I doubt Rae knows 
about the Academy Knights.

08:35.640 --> 08:37.280
Oh, I guess not.

08:38.440 --> 08:42.790
The Academy Knights resolve 
conflicts between students,

08:42.790 --> 08:45.690
kill monsters on the grounds, 
that kind of thing.

08:45.690 --> 08:48.990
They're basically an autonomous 
organization within the academy.

08:49.290 --> 08:53.720
It's deeply rooted in tradition, and only 
the elite who pass the exam can join.

08:53.720 --> 08:56.290
I think it'd be worth trying.

08:56.290 --> 08:58.430
<i>The Academy Knights...</i>

08:58.430 --> 09:02.460
<i>I mean, they were in the game, 
so of course I know about them.</i>

09:02.460 --> 09:06.090
<i>They go by the name "Knights," 
but it's basically the student council.</i>

09:03.060 --> 09:05.230
<b>Times like these are pretty nice, right?</b>

09:03.060 --> 09:05.270
<b>Rod</b>

09:05.350 --> 09:07.480
<b>Thane</b>

09:05.350 --> 09:07.480
<b>Unbound by duty and status...
Looks like there's still more I could learn from you.</b>

09:06.090 --> 09:10.850
<i>If you join, you get to see some 
exclusive event CGs of the princes...</i>

09:07.600 --> 09:10.150
<b>Yu</b>

09:07.600 --> 09:10.150
<b>Let's both do our best together!!</b>

09:10.850 --> 09:14.440
<i>but as far as the game goes, I don't 
really care whether I'm in it or not.</i>

09:14.740 --> 09:16.840
What, not interested?

09:16.840 --> 09:19.950
I thought you'd jump at the chance.

09:19.950 --> 09:21.870
Eh... I don't...

09:21.870 --> 09:26.230
Then you could be like, "I'm the knight 
who protects Miss Claire!"

09:26.230 --> 09:28.710
<i>The knight who protects Miss Claire?!</i>

09:30.980 --> 09:34.210
A villain! Someone help me!

09:34.210 --> 09:35.920
My lady!

09:41.630 --> 09:42.910
My lady...

09:43.200 --> 09:46.940
Oh, my knight...

09:46.940 --> 09:48.310
I'll do it!

09:48.310 --> 09:51.520
I don't even want to know 
what you were just imagining,

09:51.520 --> 09:53.980
but I'll be taking the exam, as well.

09:53.980 --> 09:54.650
Huh?

09:55.090 --> 09:57.900
So sorry your plan didn't 
work out as you had hoped.

09:58.430 --> 10:00.660
<i>Does that mean...</i>

10:00.660 --> 10:02.160
Put me down!

10:02.160 --> 10:05.580
I can't have you protecting me 
for the rest of my life!

10:07.420 --> 10:09.940
I can fight, too!

10:10.870 --> 10:13.500
You're imagining something weird again!

10:14.170 --> 10:15.220
Watch it!

10:22.980 --> 10:24.750
Is it me, or is the ground shaking?

10:28.380 --> 10:30.600
What's going on?

10:30.600 --> 10:32.480
H-Hey!

10:32.480 --> 10:33.630
An earthquake?

10:36.900 --> 10:38.070
<i>A monster!</i>

10:53.000 --> 10:55.500
Monster! It's a monster!

10:55.880 --> 10:57.300
A water slime?

10:57.300 --> 10:59.220
It's unbelievably huge.

10:59.220 --> 11:02.170
If that thing swallowed you up, 
you'd be a goner.

11:04.310 --> 11:08.390
Everyone, get back! Take refuge, 
and let me handle this!

11:10.650 --> 11:12.650
Keep calm, and get to a safe distance!

11:12.650 --> 11:14.400
This way, everyone!

11:27.730 --> 11:30.110
Hey! What are you doing?!

11:30.110 --> 11:31.980
You need to start running, too!

11:31.980 --> 11:33.120
Commoner!

11:35.350 --> 11:37.590
Hey! Take refuge, quickly!

11:37.590 --> 11:39.840
That monster's a water type.

11:39.840 --> 11:44.080
You can't use the wind magic 
that's strong against it, can you?

11:39.840 --> 11:44.090
<b>Water</b>

11:39.840 --> 11:44.090
<b>Wind</b>

11:39.840 --> 11:44.090
<b>Fire</b>

11:39.840 --> 11:44.090
<b>Earth</b>

11:44.080 --> 11:45.620
Well, no, but...

11:45.620 --> 11:47.210
I'll help you!

11:58.530 --> 12:02.460
How can you construct such 
impressive magic walls so quickly?

12:02.460 --> 12:04.540
You're no beginner at this!

12:04.540 --> 12:07.530
<i>Well, yes, naturally I've already 
accounted for all this!</i>

12:07.530 --> 12:10.720
<i>This is a monster attack event 
that happens in the game.</i>

12:07.530 --> 12:11.410
<b>A water slime draws near!</b>

12:07.530 --> 12:14.790
<b>m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100</b>

12:07.530 --> 12:14.790
<b>m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100</b>

12:07.530 --> 12:14.790
<b>m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100</b>

12:07.530 --> 12:14.790
<b>Fight 
Item 
Talk 
Plan 
Run</b>

12:07.530 --> 12:14.790
<b>Mud Lance</b>

12:10.720 --> 12:14.790
<i>I've been secretly practicing 
my magic just for this day.</i>

12:11.410 --> 12:12.790
<b>The water slime took 35 damage!</b>

12:12.790 --> 12:13.670
<b>The water slime took 38 damage!</b>

12:13.670 --> 12:14.790
<b>The water slime took 42 damage!</b>

12:14.790 --> 12:17.240
<i>Once I got used to it, I improved quickly.</i>

12:17.240 --> 12:20.550
<i>Thanks, protag specs!</i>

12:21.100 --> 12:23.560
Mr. Torrid! Give everyone 
the order to attack!

12:23.560 --> 12:25.610
We can overpower it with numbers now!

12:25.610 --> 12:26.990
R-Right!

12:26.990 --> 12:31.460
Everyone! Use your attack magic 
together on my signal!

12:54.650 --> 12:57.610
Aim through the cracks 
between the earth walls!

12:59.960 --> 13:01.210
Fire!

13:08.970 --> 13:10.260
Did we get it?

13:11.950 --> 13:13.040
<i>No...</i>

13:13.850 --> 13:16.080
<i>That just set a flag.</i>

13:24.070 --> 13:26.250
Everyone, keep your wits about you!

13:26.250 --> 13:29.950
This is the Hateful Cry! 
Monsters use it to threaten their foes!

13:29.950 --> 13:31.050
Damn it!

13:31.050 --> 13:33.040
I can't even move!

13:33.450 --> 13:34.750
<i>This is bad!</i>

13:34.750 --> 13:39.060
<i>Even Prince Rod and 
Prince Yu are immobilized!</i>

13:46.800 --> 13:47.860
<i>Oh, no!</i>

13:47.860 --> 13:50.610
<i>I used too much magic on those walls! 
I've got none left!</i>

14:04.050 --> 14:08.820
<i>No! This is about to end up 
just like it does in the game!</i>

14:08.820 --> 14:10.820
<b>Rod</b>

14:08.820 --> 14:10.870
<b>Close call, huh? But it's okay now.
I'll finish this thing off.</b>

14:09.220 --> 14:10.840
<i>During this event in the game,</i>

14:10.840 --> 14:12.780
<i>when the heroine is in danger,</i>

14:10.870 --> 14:12.700
<b>Thane</b>

14:10.870 --> 14:12.700
<b>Are you all right? Leave the rest to me.
This is my job now!</b>

14:12.780 --> 14:15.000
<b>Just in the nick of time! You're safe now.
I'll take care of the rest!</b>

14:12.780 --> 14:15.450
<b>Yu</b>

14:12.780 --> 14:15.570
<i>the romanceable characters 
gallantly save her...</i>

14:17.060 --> 14:18.710
<i>I see something!</i>

14:18.710 --> 14:20.710
<b>Rod</b>

14:18.710 --> 14:20.710
<b>Thane</b>

14:18.710 --> 14:20.710
<b>Yu</b>

14:20.710 --> 14:23.240
<i>No! I don't wanna make this choice!</i>

14:23.240 --> 14:26.910
<i>It'll set a flag! Someone's 
affection level will skyrocket!</i>

14:26.050 --> 14:33.310
<b>Rod</b>

14:26.050 --> 14:33.310
<b>Thane</b>

14:26.050 --> 14:33.310
<b>Yu</b>

14:26.910 --> 14:30.580
<i>I need different options 
that aren't the princes!</i>

14:30.580 --> 14:33.310
<i>If there was a name I'd want to call out...</i>

14:33.310 --> 14:34.970
<b>Yu</b>

14:34.310 --> 14:35.930
Save me,

14:34.970 --> 14:35.930
<b>Yu</b>

14:34.970 --> 14:35.930
<b>Claire</b>

14:35.930 --> 14:37.930
Miss Claire!

14:37.930 --> 14:39.690
Huh?!

14:41.730 --> 14:43.950
<i>Oh, right... In this scene...</i>

14:43.950 --> 14:47.270
<i>Miss Claire's also been caught by a tentacle.</i>

14:46.110 --> 14:50.030
<b>Thane</b>

14:46.110 --> 14:50.030
<b>Are you all right? Leave the rest to me.
This is my job now!</b>

14:47.270 --> 14:50.570
<i>She shows up in Prince Thane's event CG!</i>

14:50.570 --> 14:53.450
<i>It's a tiny image, but it's so cute!</i>

14:58.150 --> 14:59.080
Miss Claire!

15:01.240 --> 15:04.570
Ugh! Could this monster 
be any more barbaric?

15:06.290 --> 15:09.010
I'm still feeling the effects 
of its Hateful Cry...

15:10.320 --> 15:12.670
I can't save anyone this way...

15:12.670 --> 15:15.170
Stay strong, Claire François.

15:18.940 --> 15:20.270
Prince Thane!

15:20.270 --> 15:22.770
<b>Damage</b>

15:23.650 --> 15:25.170
I'll back you up.

15:25.170 --> 15:27.740
Hit it with all the magic you've got.

15:27.740 --> 15:30.520
B-But my attribute is fire.

15:30.520 --> 15:32.660
It won't affect a water-type monster.

15:33.030 --> 15:35.660
It's all right. I know you can do it.

15:38.660 --> 15:39.740
Right!

15:41.240 --> 15:42.790
We hit it with full power!

15:42.790 --> 15:44.320
Of course!

15:53.530 --> 15:56.070
You caught me by surprise before,

15:56.070 --> 15:58.760
but you won't be so lucky this time!

16:12.610 --> 16:14.840
Awesome! Dashing! Beautiful!

16:14.840 --> 16:17.370
I love you so much, Miss Claire!

16:21.830 --> 16:25.180
Miss Claire! Do it!

16:25.940 --> 16:27.390
Roar forth!

16:27.390 --> 16:28.890
Clad in the breeze!

16:29.500 --> 16:31.250
Flame Lance!

16:31.730 --> 16:33.840
Enchant Wind!

17:17.240 --> 17:18.540
Are you all right?

17:23.200 --> 17:25.520
I-I'm so sorry!

17:28.360 --> 17:29.270
It's—

17:37.990 --> 17:39.390
Ow...

17:42.210 --> 17:43.180
You saved us!

17:43.180 --> 17:45.080
That was amazing, Miss Claire!

17:43.600 --> 17:45.080
Incredible!

17:45.080 --> 17:48.460
I can't believe you took out such 
an enormous monster in one hit!

17:48.460 --> 17:51.850
B-But it wasn't just me...

17:57.690 --> 17:59.470
Oh, there you are.

18:05.480 --> 18:08.480
It's okay. You don't need to be afraid.

18:09.090 --> 18:09.990
Come on.

18:15.490 --> 18:18.400
That was your mommy back there, wasn't it?

18:18.870 --> 18:21.450
She was fighting to protect you, wasn't she?

18:28.840 --> 18:30.140
I'm sorry.

18:31.450 --> 18:34.470
I'll be your mommy instead.

18:34.890 --> 18:37.660
We'll forge the Familiar Pact right now.

18:41.330 --> 18:43.550
Your name is Ralaire now.

18:44.890 --> 18:46.870
Let's be friends, Ralaire.

18:52.310 --> 18:54.150
Hey, that tickles!

19:02.890 --> 19:03.910
Prince Thane!

19:10.360 --> 19:13.920
Um... I wanted to thank you.

19:13.920 --> 19:18.280
If not for you, I don't know 
what would've happened to me.

19:20.930 --> 19:25.350
I'm sure you would have handled 
things just fine without me.

19:25.350 --> 19:27.430
Th-That's not...

19:28.440 --> 19:29.430
But still...

19:33.060 --> 19:34.560
You did well.

19:43.640 --> 19:45.490
C-Commoner!

19:45.490 --> 19:47.570
Where have you been?!

19:47.570 --> 19:49.870
Were you hurt?! Are you all right?!

19:51.670 --> 19:54.190
Oh... Yes. I'm just fine.

19:54.190 --> 19:56.630
But should you have done that?

19:56.630 --> 19:58.630
Huh? Done what?

19:58.630 --> 20:02.850
Well... You just snapped 
the flag you set in half...

20:02.850 --> 20:05.700
What in the world are you talking about?

20:05.700 --> 20:08.150
Do you know how worried I—

20:08.150 --> 20:11.880
It's happened! You're finally 
getting all affectionate!

20:13.140 --> 20:14.860
I am <i>not</i>!

20:14.860 --> 20:17.610
Where do you keep getting 
that idea, anyway?!

20:20.670 --> 20:24.070
Well, for a commoner, you did quite well.

20:24.070 --> 20:24.860
Huh?

20:25.820 --> 20:27.380
I'm saying...

20:27.380 --> 20:31.830
You did a good job keeping 
the monster in one place.

20:37.150 --> 20:39.490
Rae! Miss Claire!

20:39.840 --> 20:41.930
Come on, let's hurry back already.

22:36.790 --> 22:39.790
Oh, sure. Just a sec.

22:42.540 --> 22:44.490
You've got quite the appetite.

22:45.560 --> 22:46.260
Hey!

22:47.760 --> 22:49.430
Ow, ow, ow...

22:49.430 --> 22:52.850
Y-You're full of curiosity, too. 
You're gonna need trai—

22:52.850 --> 22:53.930
Hang on...

22:54.840 --> 22:57.740
That's a monster, isn't it?

22:58.540 --> 23:01.390
Calm down, Misha! Just listen! Hear me out!

23:01.390 --> 23:03.060
I <i>am</i> calm!

23:03.440 --> 23:05.810
And help me train this little one!

23:05.810 --> 23:09.470
Could you not just dump a headache 
like that on me so naturally?

23:12.780 --> 23:14.720
H-How cute...

23:14.720 --> 23:15.540
Gotcha!

23:16.000 --> 23:18.680
<i>So, with Misha's help,</i>

23:18.680 --> 23:22.310
<i>I then started the process 
of training Ralaire, but...</i>

23:25.160 --> 23:28.710
Hey, commoner! Where did you put my brush?

23:28.710 --> 23:30.270
Lene is looking fo—

23:37.000 --> 23:38.420
A monster...

23:46.660 --> 23:48.750
The first part of the knight 
exam is the written part!

23:49.480 --> 23:51.010
This'll be easy!

23:51.010 --> 23:55.120
People always get their answers off 
by one when filling these out, huh?

23:55.120 --> 23:57.950
Y-You don't mean... Me, of all people?!

23:57.950 --> 24:00.580
Why don't we compare 
our answers, Miss Claire?

23:59.500 --> 24:01.000
<b>Episode 5</b>

23:59.500 --> 24:01.000
<b>The Knight Exam Is Packed with Drama</b>
